            mir_ins_t: `What your programme shows`,
            ins_mandate: `You installed the founder’s full system by fiat. A firm that runs this model hires for it and onboards for months; you imposed it in one step on 640 people who joined a different company. The week-2 numbers looked like success because people perform for the camera; the pulse survey and the resignations showed the cost.`,
            ins_courage: `Your diagnosis put {c} of 100 points on skill and nerve. The evidence pointed elsewhere: 11 of 14 described the defect correctly, and the senior engineer was not afraid. Silence came from the expected cost of speaking and from having no route to the decision.`,
            ins_volume: `Your dashboard counted activity. Ratings and logged issues rise as soon as people learn they are counted, while the number of risks that really reach a decision-maker can fall. You were steering by the wrong instrument.`,
            ins_traits: `You rated people, not ideas. Feedback aimed at the self raises its image cost: people stop asking for it and stop exposing half-formed concerns. Rating decisions and arguments gets the candour without the threat.`,
            ins_believe: `You weighted votes by believability without a track record. With no data on who called past decisions right, the weights encoded seniority and confidence, and the juniors who saw Quaybook coming lost their voice.`,
            ins_suspend: `You switched the app off the day someone used it to challenge the system with data. Everyone learned what happens to candour aimed upward, and escalation stalled.`,
            ins_scale: `Scaling to everyone on 1 May repeated the original error: people who never opted in got the full system, and the units that joined by mandate rebuilt their side channels.`,
            ins_record: `You recorded nearly everything and protected few zones of privacy. Observation that total drives real thinking into private messages: the transparency paradox.`,
            ins_trap: `You took go/no-go meetings off the record to let people speak freely. That is the one meeting where a recorded objection matters most; Quaybook was approved in a meeting with no minutes.`,
            ins_resign: `“Sign or leave” turned a culture change into a loyalty test. The people with the most options left first.`,
            ins_keep: `You thanked Dana and left the ratings unchanged. Praising candour while ignoring its content teaches people that speaking up changes nothing.`,
            ins_anon: `Anonymous ratings removed accountability: scores got harsher and the bias grew, with no one to answer for it.`,
            ins_defend: `Standing by a recording made without consent turned a fixable mistake into a legal and commercial dispute.`,
            ins_stop: `Stopping the programme left the original problem in place: 2 of 14 still speak up, and the next Quaybook has the same odds.`,
            ins_hold: `Your design was healthy at week 10, but you held it at the pilot. The units outside it kept the January silence for another year.`,
            ins_adapt_sick: `You extended a design that was failing at week 10. Extending it spread the side channels and the bias to the units that joined.`,
            ins_screen: `A personality screen for candour selects for confidence, not for the willingness to report a risk, and invites legal challenge.`,
            ins_nostop: `You set no stop condition. Without one, the board has no way to tell a slow start from harm.`,
            ins_good_diag: `Your diagnosis matched the evidence: the cost of speaking and the missing route explained the silence, not a lack of nerve.`,
